
<section class="mb-10 rounded-[28px] border-2 border-orange-100 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50/80 via-white to-emerald-50/60 p-5 sm:p-7">
  <div class="mb-7">
    <p class="text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-600">
      Administrator learning guide
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-black text-slate-800 sm:text-3xl">
      Understand the investigation lifecycle
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
      A workspace preserves a research effort as it develops. These stages
      describe how to use the library; the actual status of each investigation
      comes from its saved database record.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="relative px-1 sm:px-3">
    <div class="absolute left-[8%] right-[8%] top-8 hidden h-2 rounded-full bg-orange-100 md:block"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-4">
      <article class="relative z-10 rounded-3xl border-2 border-orange-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-[22px] border-[3px] border-orange-400 bg-orange-50 text-2xl font-black text-orange-700 ring-4 ring-orange-100">
          01
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-black text-orange-800">Continue</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700">Active investigations</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Use this stage for work that still needs investigation, additional
          research items, evidence collection, annotations, or decisions.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-2xl bg-orange-50 p-4 text-base leading-7 text-orange-900">
          <strong>Administrator tip:</strong> Check the outstanding items and
          the quality of supporting evidence before moving the investigation forward.
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="relative z-10 rounded-3xl border-2 border-sky-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-[22px] border-[3px] border-sky-300 bg-sky-50 text-2xl font-black text-sky-700 ring-4 ring-sky-100">
          02
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-black text-sky-800">Review</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700">Completed investigations</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Consult previously completed work, revisit recorded conclusions,
          and examine the research items and evidence preserved with the workspace.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-2xl bg-sky-50 p-4 text-base leading-7 text-sky-900">
          <strong>Administrator tip:</strong> Completed describes the recorded
          workflow state; it does not independently prove that every conclusion is correct.
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="relative z-10 rounded-3xl border-2 border-violet-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-[22px] border-[3px] border-violet-300 bg-violet-50 text-2xl font-black text-violet-700 ring-4 ring-violet-100">
          03
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-black text-violet-800">Retrieve</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700">Archived investigations</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Locate work that has been set aside but remains useful as historical
          context, a source of prior findings, or a reference for future research.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-2xl bg-violet-50 p-4 text-base leading-7 text-violet-900">
          <strong>Administrator tip:</strong> Archiving is an organizational
          action. Do not assume it deletes a record or guarantees that every related
          object has been retained.
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>